{"title":"Career Roadmap · Quantity Surveyor","role":"Quantity Surveyor","summary":"A Quantity Surveyor (QS) manages the commercial and contractual side of construction projects—estimating quantities, preparing BOQs, costing materials and labour, evaluating tenders, tracking project costs, valuing work completed, managing variations, and supporting contracts and claims.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Civil Engineering is one of the strongest direct undergraduate pathways into quantity surveying because it provides the required understanding of construction methods, drawings, materials, specifications, measurements and project execution."},{"type":"note","label":"Career positioning","text":"Quantity Surveyor is generally an entry-level to mid-career profession, unlike roles such as Commercial Manager or Senior Quantity Surveyor, which normally require several years of experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Typical development","What you should build"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Civil Engineering + QS foundation"},{"text":"Estimation, costing, quantity take-off, BOQ, AutoCAD, Excel"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Graduate / Assistant Quantity Surveyor → Quantity Surveyor"},{"text":"Measurement, procurement, valuations, contracts, variations"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior QS / Commercial QS"},{"text":"Contract administration, claims, cost control, commercial strategy"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Commercial Manager / Contracts Manager / Cost Consultant"},{"text":"Leadership, major-project commercial management, digital QS"}]]}]},{"heading":"Build the Right Skills During B.Tech","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Basic construction materials"},{"text":"Introduction to civil engineering"},{"text":"Basic surveying"},{"text":"Computer fundamentals"},{"text":"Excel fundamentals"},{"text":"Technical communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start developing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Excel"},{"text":"AutoCAD fundamentals"},{"text":"Construction terminology"},{"text":"Reading architectural and structural drawings"},{"text":"Basic measurement concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mini project"},{"type":"h","text":"Residential Building Quantity Take-Off"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Floor plans"},{"text":"Area calculations"},{"text":"Concrete quantities"},{"text":"Brickwork quantities"},{"text":"Plaster quantities"},{"text":"Flooring quantities"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Output","text":"Excel quantity sheet + AutoCAD drawings."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Estimation & Quantity Measurement"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important stage for a future QS."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Building construction"},{"text":"Concrete technology"},{"text":"Structural engineering basics"},{"text":"Surveying"},{"text":"Estimation and costing"},{"text":"Construction materials"},{"text":"Construction equipment"},{"text":"Soil/foundation basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"QS skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quantity take-off"},{"text":"BOQ preparation"},{"text":"Rate analysis"},{"text":"Material estimation"},{"text":"Labour estimation"},{"text":"Measurement sheets"},{"text":"Abstract estimates"},{"text":"Cost comparison"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"MS Project basics"},{"text":"Quantity take-off software"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Complete Building Estimation"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drawing interpretation"},{"text":"Quantity take-off"},{"text":"BOQ"},{"text":"Rate analysis"},{"text":"Material requirement"},{"text":"Labour requirement"},{"text":"Total project estimate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Quantity Surveying"},{"type":"p","text":"Now move from academic estimation to commercial construction management."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Construction planning"},{"text":"Construction management"},{"text":"Contracts"},{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Tendering"},{"text":"Project scheduling"},{"text":"Cost control"},{"text":"Building services"},{"text":"Structural design fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"QS competencies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tender documentation"},{"text":"Bid comparison"},{"text":"Contractor quotation analysis"},{"text":"Interim payment valuation"},{"text":"Variation measurement"},{"text":"Cost reporting"},{"text":"Budget tracking"},{"text":"Subcontractor measurement"},{"text":"Material reconciliation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software stack"},{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Priority"],"rows":[[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"CostX / similar QS software"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"MS Project / Primavera"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"BIM / Revit"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"★★★☆☆"}],[{"text":"ERP / procurement systems"},{"text":"★★★☆☆"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Major project"},{"type":"h","text":"Commercial Management of a G+5 Building"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BOQ"},{"text":"Tender"},{"text":"Contractor comparison"},{"text":"Project budget"},{"text":"Cost plan"},{"text":"Monthly valuation"},{"text":"Variation register"},{"text":"Cost-to-complete report"},{"text":"Final account"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Industry-Ready Quantity Surveyor"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on becoming employable rather than learning only theory."},{"type":"h","text":"Master"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bills of quantities"},{"text":"Tendering"},{"text":"Rate analysis"},{"text":"Contract administration"},{"text":"Interim payment certificates"},{"text":"Variation orders"},{"text":"Claims"},{"text":"Final accounts"},{"text":"Cost forecasting"},{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Subcontract management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn contract frameworks"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FIDIC"},{"text":"NEC"},{"text":"EPC contracts"},{"text":"Design & Build"},{"text":"Lump-sum contracts"},{"text":"Item-rate contracts"},{"text":"Cost-plus contracts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-year project"},{"type":"h","text":"End-to-End Quantity Surveying for a Commercial Building"},{"type":"p","text":"Deliver:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Architectural Drawings","Quantity Take-Off","BOQ","Rate Analysis","Tender","Bid Comparison","Contract","Progress Measurement","Interim Valuation","Variations","Cost Control","Final Account"]},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes a strong portfolio project for QS applications."}]},{"heading":"Four-Year Skill Development","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Technical","Commercial","Software","Portfolio"],"rows":[[{"text":"1"},{"text":"Civil fundamentals"},{"text":"Basic costing"},{"text":"Excel, AutoCAD"},{"text":"Building quantities"}],[{"text":"2"},{"text":"Estimation"},{"text":"BOQ & rate analysis"},{"text":"Excel, AutoCAD"},{"text":"Building estimate"}],[{"text":"3"},{"text":"Construction management"},{"text":"Tendering & contracts"},{"text":"MS Project, BIM/QS tools"},{"text":"Commercial project"}],[{"text":"4"},{"text":"Advanced construction"},{"text":"Claims, variations, final accounts"},{"text":"Advanced Excel, BIM, Power BI"},{"text":"Complete QS project"}]]}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After gaining foundational QS knowledge, you can specialise."},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Main Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Building Quantity Surveying"},{"text":"Residential/commercial b